  "step_3": "The decision reason is about preferring a lottery that is more right-skewed — meaning more probability on unfavorable outcomes. However, in this case, Lottery A has a 20% chance of 0€ (unfavorable), which is relatively low, and 80% of 4000€ (favorable), so it is actually left-skewed. Lottery B has no unfavorable outcomes. Therefore, neither lottery is right-skewed, so the reason does not apply. The individual’s justification is based on the certainty and high payoff of B, not on skewness or unfavorable outcomes. There is no mention of skewness, unfavorable outcomes, or any evaluation of the distribution in terms of risk in the direction of unfavorable outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual’s reasoning is entirely different — it is based on expected value and certainty, not on skewness. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
